{"nodes":[{"id":"sec-opening","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":0,"width":420,"height":180},{"id":"sec-love","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":260,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#What we mean by “love” ❤️"},{"id":"sec-sex","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":520,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Talk about making love before you do it"},{"id":"sec-readiness","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":780,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Should you be in a relationship at all?"},{"id":"sec-finding","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":1040,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"##How to find a partner"},{"id":"sec-starting","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":1300,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Starting on the right foot"},{"id":"sec-crucible","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":1560,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Are you ready for the crucible?"},{"id":"sec-maturity","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":1820,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"##When you and your partner are at different levels of maturity"},{"id":"sec-primal","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":2080,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Primal attraction: channeling the Divine Masculine & Feminine"},{"id":"sec-twin","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":2340,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Twin Flames?"},{"id":"sec-community","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":2600,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Two Pillars Don't Hold The Roof Up"},{"id":"sec-choosing","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":2860,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#What are you actually choosing together?"},{"id":"sec-conscious","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":3120,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Doing it consciously 🧭"},{"id":"sec-already","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":3380,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#If you’re already in it"},{"id":"sec-children","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":3640,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Children"},{"id":"sec-ending","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":3900,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Ending consciously"},{"id":"sec-tough","type":"file","file":"articles/romance/master.md","x":0,"y":4160,"width":420,"height":180,"subpath":"#Tough Love"},{"id":"q-G001","type":"text","text":"## G001 — partial\n\nHow do I know this relationship is actually becoming healthier over time, rather than merely becoming deeper, more intense, or more entangled?\n\n**Importance:** high  \n**Disposition:** review\n\nThe article supplies many ingredients—honesty, trust, self-regulation, outside support, agape, community—but no explicit longitudinal success test.","x":620,"y":1560,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-G002","type":"text","text":"## G002 — partial\n\nHow do I distinguish a repairable trigger or growth edge from a fundamental incompatibility—or from a relationship that is simply unsafe?\n\n**Importance:** high  \n**Disposition:** review\n\nDanger receives a clear safety boundary, and incompatibility appears throughout, but the middle category—painful yet workable versus structurally wrong—remains distributed rather than resolved.","x":620,"y":1770,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-G003","type":"text","text":"## G003 — partial\n\nAfter an ordinary fight, what does a successful repair actually look like?\n\n**Importance:** medium-high  \n**Disposition:** review\n\nThe article asks how a prospective partner repaired past conflicts and later offers several repair ingredients, but there is no compact ordinary-conflict repair sequence.","x":620,"y":1300,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-G004","type":"text","text":"## G004 — partial\n\nHow much mismatch can two people realistically work through before 'growth' becomes an excuse for incompatibility?\n\n**Importance:** high  \n**Disposition:** review\n\nThe draft distinguishes complementarity, maturity gaps, sexual fit, values, and irreconcilable memories, but not a general decision rule—which may or may not be desirable.","x":620,"y":1820,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-G005","type":"text","text":"## G005 — partial\n\nWhile I am inside the relationship, how can I tell durable romantic love from attachment, idealization, trauma activation, or simply wanting to be wanted?\n\n**Importance:** high  \n**Disposition:** review\n\nThis distinction is central to several sections but remains a distributed argument rather than a reader-facing discriminant.","x":620,"y":1510,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-G006","type":"text","text":"## G006 — thin\n\nOnce children actually arrive, how do we keep the romantic relationship alive while parenting, rather than only planning for children or protecting them if we separate?\n\n**Importance:** high  \n**Disposition:** review\n\nChildren are a recurring organizing test from the opening onward, but the dedicated Children section concentrates on obligations and breakup/co-parenting.","x":620,"y":3640,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-G007","type":"text","text":"## G007 — thin\n\nBefore merging lives, what should couples actually work out about money, labor, dependency, and household responsibility?\n\n**Importance:** medium  \n**Disposition:** review-or-scope\n\nThe article repeatedly uses money, provision, work, housing, and resentment as examples but does not develop a practical treatment of shared logistics.","x":620,"y":2860,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-G008","type":"text","text":"## G008 — partial\n\nWhat is the difference between a healthy boundary and an attempt to control or punish a partner?\n\n**Importance:** medium  \n**Disposition:** review\n\nBoundaries, demands, consent, exclusivity, coercion, and safety all appear, but the distinction itself is not made explicit.","x":620,"y":1980,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-C001","type":"text","text":"## C001 — answered\n\nIf I do not already have a commune or shared community, what can I practically do now?\n\n**Importance:** high  \n**Disposition:** no-gap\n\nThe Two Pillars section answers this directly with mutual friendships, meetups, shared purpose, and partial community-building.","x":1260,"y":2600,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-C002","type":"text","text":"## C002 — answered-next\n\nWhat if we are already deeply entangled or married, so the advice to slow down comes too late?\n\n**Importance:** high  \n**Disposition:** no-gap\n\nThe article anticipates this question and immediately opens the next major section with it.","x":1260,"y":3120,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-C003","type":"text","text":"## C003 — answered-partially-by-design\n\nWhat if sexual compatibility or libido changes after we are already bonded?\n\n**Importance:** medium  \n**Disposition:** no-gap\n\nThe early sex section explicitly recommends discussing later divergence before either person is hurt; later material treats fit as partly discoverable only through experience.","x":1260,"y":520,"width":520,"height":190},{"id":"q-C004","type":"text","text":"## C004 — answered\n\nHow do I avoid making my partner my entire emotional and social world?\n\n**Importance:** high  \n**Disposition:** no-gap\n\nThe article gives a dedicated section and later community treatment.","x":1260,"y":2190,"width":520,"height":190}],"edges":[{"id":"edge-flow-opening-love","fromNode":"sec-opening","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-love","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-love-sex","fromNode":"sec-love","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-sex","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-sex-readiness","fromNode":"sec-sex","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-readiness","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-readiness-finding","fromNode":"sec-readiness","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-finding","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-finding-starting","fromNode":"sec-finding","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-starting","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-starting-crucible","fromNode":"sec-starting","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-crucible","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-crucible-maturity","fromNode":"sec-crucible","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-maturity","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-maturity-primal","fromNode":"sec-maturity","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-primal","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-primal-twin","fromNode":"sec-primal","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-twin","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-twin-community","fromNode":"sec-twin","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-community","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-community-choosing","fromNode":"sec-community","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-choosing","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-choosing-conscious","fromNode":"sec-choosing","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-conscious","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-conscious-already","fromNode":"sec-conscious","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-already","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-already-children","fromNode":"sec-already","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-children","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-children-ending","fromNode":"sec-children","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-ending","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-flow-ending-tough","fromNode":"sec-ending","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sec-tough","toSide":"top","label":"article flow"},{"id":"edge-raise-G001","fromNode":"sec-crucible","fromSide":"right","toNode":"q-G001","toSide":"left","label":"raises / exposes"},{"id":"edge-answer-G001-0","fromNode":"sec-crucible","fro